     "acute",
     "obtuse",
     "protractor"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Angles appear in clock hands, scissors, doors and roofs. A door opening a little makes an acute angle and a wide open door makes an obtuse angle.\nTo draw an angle of 50 degrees, draw a base line, place the protractor centre on one end, mark 50 on the scale and join the mark to the vertex.\nTwo angles that add up to 90 degrees are complementary. Two that add up to 180 degrees are supplementary."
    }
